# ── LBD games ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dev-only dependencies. Neither game needs node_modules at RUNTIME (LBD 2 loads
# a vendored js/vendor/gsap.min.js; LBD 1 is a single inline index.html), so 28MB
# of it should not ship with the book.
LBD/*/node_modules/

# ⚠ NOT SOLVED BY THIS FILE — read before committing:
# Each game folder still carries its OWN .git directory, so `git add` stages it as
# an embedded repository ("gitlink") instead of the files:
#     warning: adding embedded git repository: LBD/Glass half full LBD 1
# A clone or a Vercel deploy of THIS repo would then contain two EMPTY game
# folders, and both game pages would come up blank. Ignoring the nested .git does
# not change that — git decides on the presence of .git on disk.
# To actually ship the games, their nested .git directories have to go:
#     rm -rf "LBD/Glass half full LBD 1/.git" "LBD/Glass half full LBD 2/.git"
# Checked before suggesting it: both are fully pushed (HEAD == origin/main, no
# uncommitted files, no unpushed commits) to
#   github.com/yuvrajsingh-alt/THE-GLASS-HALF-FULL
#   github.com/harshvishnu4-cpu/Glass-Half-full-LBD-2-
# so the history survives on those remotes and the folders can be re-cloned.
# That also drops the book's LBD payload from 204MB to about 22MB.
